ure":"none","reveal_animation":"stagger"}},"stellar_product_faq_Ca6FUY":{"type":"stellar-product-faq","blocks":{"faq_eNHnCt":{"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"What is Nova?","answer":"Nova is an over-the-counter antacid for the relief of heartburn, acid indigestion, and sour stomach. \n\nEach chewable tablet delivers 1,500 mg of calcium carbonate in a mild strawberry flavor. Every order includes two travel sleeves and eight blister cards. Each blister card contains eight tablets."}},"faq_9YU6fP":{"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"How does Nova work?","answer":"Nova works by neutralizing excess acid in your stomach, providing quick relief from heartburn and acid indigestion. Calcium carbonate is the active ingredient in Nova, which is a natural alkaline compound.\n\nWhen you chew and swallow Nova, the calcium carbonate balances the excess acid in your stomach. This prevents stomach acid from reaching your esophagus, which can cause irritation and burning."}},"faq_YJJmaj":{"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"How and when should I take Nova?","answer":"Chew 1 - 2 Nova tablets as you experience symptoms."}},"faq_q4qhx6":{"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Is Nova FDA approved?","answer":"Nova is regulated by the FDA. Nova complies with the Code of Federal Regulations for Antacid Products for Over-the-Counter use, just like Tums, Rolaids, Alka-Seltzer, and other leading store brand antacids."}},"faq_xtdbKL":{"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"What is in Nova?","answer":"The main active ingredient in Nova is calcium carbonate.\n\nNova is free from: sugar, dyes, preservatives, gluten, and talc. Nova contains strawberry flavor, sucralose and xylitol for sweetness, and magnesium stearate and povidone as binding agents."}}},"block_order":["faq_eNHnCt","faq_9YU6fP","faq_YJJmaj","faq_q4qhx6","faq_xtdbKL"],"custom_css":["h2 {color: #ffffff;}"],"name":"Stellar Product FAQ","settings":{"heading":"Frequently Asked Questions","padding_top":4,"padding_bottom":4,"color_sch